  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 217 AM EDT Thu May 28 2026\n\nWeak front was slowly making its way SE across the\nforecast area with dewpoints in the low 60s ahead of it and mid\nto upper 50 in its wake. The few showers/storms that came close\nto NE Hillsdale county have dissipated. The overall sfc flow \nwill become NE and persist for the next couple of days, allowing\ndrier and slightly cooler air to filter in. \n\nConcerns for high swim risk and small craft conditions, which\nwere already on the marginal side at this time yesterday, appear\nto be even more questionable given the overall weak flow that\nmay increase somewhat during the day Thursday. While the\nargument can be made to drop both headlines (which GRR has \nrecently done to our north), will keep things in place overnight\nand let the day shift assess conditions after sunrise. \n\nOutside of the beach/marine issues, no real weather concerns as\ntrough pushes east of the region and a NW to SE omega block \ntakes hold into at least Saturday night with seasonable \ntemperatures and comfortable humidity. Upper level heights \nattempt to lower somewhat Sunday into Sunday night in response \nto a stronger disturbance moving through central Ontario. \nAnother front may accompany this trough, but little overall \nimpact is expected. Med range models suggest the omega block \nwill weaken, but much of the midwest and western lakes will \nremain dry through the period even as the flow aloft becomes \nsemi zonal by mid week.",
